{{!< default}}
{{!-- ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
     resources.hbs — the /resources/ index. Composed: abstract/collections.md
     §06 records "no archetype — compose; .ns-card grid or .ns-table".
     ------------------------------------------------------------------------
     ⚠ THE THIRD SILENT FALLBACK. Live routes.yaml mounts /resources/ with
     `template: resources`; the file did not exist, so Ghost served
     index.hbs. That one at least rendered its empty state rather than a
     wrong grid, which is why it looked less broken than /courses/ and
     /docs/ without being any more correct.

     ── GRID, NOT TABLE ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────
     §06 offers both. A table is right when every row shares the same handful
     of comparable columns — version, size, format. Nothing in the tag
     registry supplies those yet, so a table would be one real column
     (the name) and several empty ones, which reads as missing data rather
     than as a deliberately short row. The card grid degrades honestly:
     a resource with only a title is still a complete card.
     Revisit when §06 names the columns.

     ⚠ REUSES post-card. A resource is "is this worth opening" — the same
     question .ns-bcard already answers, so it gets the same card rather than
     a fourth near-copy of it. See the note in partials/post-card.hbs: a
     surface that needs a different card needs a different NSDS COMPONENT,
     not a copy. That is the whole of abstract/09 in one sentence.
     ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════ --}}
<section class="ns-band ns-band--tight">
    <div class="ns-band__inner">
        <div class="ns-band__head ns-band__head--between">
            <div>
                <span class="ns-kicker">{{t "// Toolkit"}}</span>
                <h1 class="ns-band__title">{{t "Resources"}}</h1>
                <p class="ns-band__lede">{{t "Cheat sheets, templates and the files worth keeping open in a second tab."}}</p>
            </div>
            <div class="ns-band__actions">
                <a class="ns-btn ns-btn--outline ns-btn--sm" href="{{@site.url}}/blog/rss/">{{> "icons/rss"}} RSS</a>
            </div>
        </div>

        {{#if posts}}
            <div class="ns-blog-grid">
                {{#foreach posts}}{{> "post-card"}}{{/foreach}}
            </div>
            {{> "pagination"}}
        {{else}}
            {{> "empty" title=(t "No resources yet")
                        text=(t "Downloads and cheat sheets will collect here.")}}
        {{/if}}
    </div>
</section>
